# FLUIDD UI Setup

This guide explains how to back up your existing Klipper configuration and install the supplied configuration files and macros.

## 1. Back Up Your Existing Configuration

In **Fluidd**, click the **Configuration** button on the left-hand side.

### Back up the KAMP folder

1. Right-click the **KAMP** folder.
2. Select **Create ZIP**.
3. Right-click the newly created ZIP file and download it to your PC.

### Back up `printer.cfg`

Right-click **`printer.cfg`** and download it to your PC.

### Back up `gcode_macro.cfg`

1. Open the **`klipper-macros-qd`** folder.
2. Right-click **`gcode_macro.cfg`**.
3. Download it to your PC.

You should now have copies of all the original, unchanged files safely stored on your PC. **Do not skip this step.**

---

## 2. Rename the Original Files

Before installing the supplied files, rename the existing configuration files so they are preserved.

Rename:


KAMP.cfg
→ KAMP.cfg-original

printer.cfg
→ printer.cfg-original

klipper-macros-qd
→ klipper-macros-qd-original

Then open the **KAMP** folder and rename:

adaptive_meshing.cfg
→ adaptive_meshing.cfg-original

KAMP_Settings.cfg
→ KAMP_Settings.cfg-original

These original files are retained as backups and can be restored if required.

---

## 3. Install the Supplied KAMP Files

Open the **KAMP** folder.

At the top of the page, click **+ ADD** and select **Upload Files**.

Upload the supplied:

adaptive_Meshing.cfg
KAMP_Settings.cfg

Once uploaded, click the blue folder icon to return to the main configuration directory.

---

## 4. Install the Main Configuration Files

Click **+ ADD** again and upload:

printer.cfg
My-Configs.cfg
gcode_macro.cfg

Once all the files have been uploaded, double-click any configuration file to open it.

In the top-right corner, click:

**SAVE & RESTART**

This will save the changes and restart Klipper.

---

## 5. Organising Macros in Fluidd

You can organise the available macros into groups to make them easier to find.

In Fluidd:

1. Click the **Settings** button on the left.
2. Scroll down to **Macros**.
3. All of the macros will be jumbled up in the "uncategorised" section.
4. Create & organise the useful macros into categorys such as: 

   * Calibration
   * Filament
   * Print

5. Click on a macro, a box will appear choose which catagory you want to put it in.
6. Only pick out the useful ones you want to use and leave the rest in the uncategorised page. 5-6 in each category.
7. They can be easily moved around to get the order you want them to be displayed

Some of the useful macros to look for are:

calabration category
PID_BED
PID_EXTRUDER
PROB_BED
SREWS_TILT
Z_TILT
PROBE_BED
ALL_HEATERS_OFF

filament category
LOAD_FILAMENT
UNLOAD_FILAMENT

print category
SET_PAUSE_AT_LAYER
CANCEL _PRINT
PAUSE
RESUME
```

Organising the macros this way gives you quick access to the functions you use most often.

---

## 6. Bed Screw Adjustment

The basic `SCREWS_TILT_CALCULATE` function is also available directly through the **Tools** section in Fluidd.
The "SCREWS_TILT" macro is a fully prepared macro of the "SCREWS_TILT_CALCULATE" function, that homes, heats the bed, heats the nozzle, wipes the nozzle before it starts.

This gives you easy access to the bed screw adjustment procedure without having to enter the command manually in the console.

The Z_TILT macro does a similar job of homeing, heating and wiping for more complete user experience than the supplied function.

---

### Important

Keep the original configuration files you downloaded as a backup. If you encounter a problem with the new configuration, you can use these files to restore your original setup.
